messages:
support-ops: FYI received a prod customer report — function call failing with a JSON schema validation error when invoking the assistant function. Happening in us-east-1. Customer says it started after SDK update.
support-ops: Raw request body they sent:
```json
{
  "name": "search_products",
  "arguments": {
    "query": {
      "keywords": ["laptop"],
      "filters": {
        "price": {
          "min": 500
        }
      }
    },
    "client_id": "acct_12345"
  }
}
```
support-ops: Response from runtime:
```json
{
  "error": {
    "type": "invalid_function_call",
    "message": "JSON schema validation error:\ninstance.path \"/arguments\": additionalProperties ['client_id'] are not allowed;\ninstance.path \"/arguments/query\": expected type \"string\" but found \"object\""
  }
}
```
jamal: Ack. Can you paste the exact SDK version and the curl they used? Is this only affecting hosted customers or Dedicated too?
ingrid: @jamal @support-ops looking — the customer is on SDK v0.9.1. That release changed how function arguments are encoded: inner objects are sent as JSON objects instead of stringifying some fields. Our function schema for search_products expects `query` to be a string (it's defined as string in the function schema). Seems like a type mismatch + an extra property `client_id` landed under `arguments` which our schema forbids (additionalProperties=false).
maria-ml: Widening the schema to accept an object feels risky for downstream evals — will change model/tool contract. Prefer to patch SDK to restore previous encoding behavior (serialize query to string) and treat this server-side as a short-term shim only.
jamal: Agreed. I'll open a canary patch on the runtime to coerce object->string for `query` when schema validation fails, log the original payload, and return a special header `X-Fn-Schema-Coerced: 1`. That gives us telemetry and a short rollback path. Also filing SDK PR to fix encoding.
jamal: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/1234 (fix: serialize nested `query` fields for function calls).
deploy-bot: deploy/runtime-canary-178214-1 started by jamal — canary targets 5% traffic in us-east-1.
sre-liz: I'll add an alert: if function call validation errors > 0.5% for 5m or p95 latency increases >100ms vs baseline, rollback the canary.
ingrid: Thanks. Support, can you ask the customer to temporarily send `query` as a JSON string (stringify) as a workaround? That should unblock them immediately.
support-ops: Replied to customer with workaround and asked for their curl. They confirmed workaround works. "Thanks!" :thumbsup:
maria-ml: Logging plan: capture original payloads that hit the coercion path and add a quick regression test against search_products to ensure downstream prompts still behave.
jamal: I'll keep the canary live for 24h while we monitor logs and merge the SDK fix. If we see any regressions we'll revert.
sre-liz: Noted — monitoring dashboards updated.
support-ops: Closing this thread once the SDK release ships. Thanks everyone.
